from (values
('127.484.d.10.F',3,'A technician who wants more hands-on training could join a local community:','["sports team only", "parade", "college program", "music band only"]'::jsonb,2,'Extended learning builds skills.','original'),
('127.484.d.10.F',4,'A student can earn a pharmacy technician certification by passing an exam such as the one given by the Pharmacy Technician Certification:','["Bakery", "Beach", "Bank", "Board"]'::jsonb,3,'PTCB offers the CPhT exam.','original'),
('127.484.d.10.G',3,'Information in a journal article is stronger when the study includes a large number of:','["participants", "pages", "ads", "pictures"]'::jsonb,0,'Sample size matters.','original'),
('127.484.d.10.G',4,'When two sources about a drug disagree, the technician should ask the pharmacist and check a:','["guess", "primary or tertiary reference", "rumor", "social post"]'::jsonb,1,'Escalate and verify.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.A',3,'Some injectable drugs must be kept cold, which is storage by:','["price", "alphabet", "temperature", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'Temperature stability matters.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.A',4,'Insulin pens in use at room temperature are labeled with a shorter use period because heat and time cause the drug to:','["gain weight", "turn into water", "become a tablet", "lose potency"]'::jsonb,3,'Heat degrades biologics.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.B',3,'A pharmacist may substitute a generic drug for a brand-name drug if the two are therapeutically:','["equivalent", "unrelated", "decorated", "expensive"]'::jsonb,0,'The Orange Book lists equivalents.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.B',4,'A product with an ''AB'' rating in the Orange Book is considered:','["banned", "therapeutically equivalent", "experimental", "unsafe"]'::jsonb,1,'AB means equivalent.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.C',3,'Removing expired items on a regular schedule is an inventory control practice often done:','["only at closing time of the year", "never", "monthly", "once in ten years"]'::jsonb,2,'Routine checks catch expired drugs.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.C',4,'A pharmacy that sets a minimum quantity at which more stock is ordered is using a(n):','["checkout line", "price tag", "coupon", "reorder point"]'::jsonb,3,'Reorder points prevent stockouts.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.D',3,'In just-in-time ordering, a pharmacy orders only small amounts when needed to reduce:','["stock on the shelf", "hand washing", "customers", "staff"]'::jsonb,0,'JIT limits inventory.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.D',4,'A drop-ship order is sent directly from the manufacturer to the:','["customer''s neighbor", "pharmacy", "post office box only", "bank"]'::jsonb,1,'Drop ship skips the wholesaler warehouse.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.E',3,'Federal law requires a special order form for purchasing Schedule II drugs, called DEA Form:','["22", "2222", "222", "2"]'::jsonb,2,'CII orders use Form 222.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.E',4,'State laws can require pharmacies to keep purchase records for at least:','["one week", "one day", "one hour", "two years"]'::jsonb,3,'Record retention laws vary by state.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.F',3,'The lot number, expiration date, and NDC on a delivery are checked against the:','["invoice", "menu", "calendar", "newspaper"]'::jsonb,0,'Checking receipts prevents errors.','original'),
('127.484.d.11.F',4,'A shipment arrives with a lot number that matches a recall. The technician should set it aside and tell the:','["bank", "pharmacist", "customers", "delivery driver only"]'::jsonb,1,'Recalled lots must not be dispensed.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.A',3,'Hand washing before handling medicines should last at least:','["2 seconds", "1 hour", "20 seconds", "5 seconds"]'::jsonb,2,'20 seconds is the standard.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.A',4,'Counting trays are cleaned between uses to prevent:','["noise", "static", "fading", "cross-contamination"]'::jsonb,3,'Residue can contaminate other drugs.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.B',3,'A material safety data sheet tells workers about the hazards of:','["chemicals", "holidays", "schedules", "paychecks"]'::jsonb,0,'SDS describes chemical hazards.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.B',4,'In a fire, the pharmacy team should follow the posted:','["price list", "evacuation plan", "menu", "sales plan"]'::jsonb,1,'Emergency plans protect people.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.C',3,'Taking drugs from the pharmacy for personal use or sale is called drug:','["donation", "delivery", "diversion", "dilution"]'::jsonb,2,'Diversion is illegal.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.C',4,'Drug diversion by an employee puts patients at risk because the missing drug may leave them without:','["signs", "ice", "paper", "treatment"]'::jsonb,3,'Patients may not receive medicine.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.D',3,'One way to minimize diversion is to keep controlled substances locked and perform regular:','["inventory counts", "parties", "raffles", "paint jobs"]'::jsonb,0,'Counts detect loss.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.D',4,'Requiring two people to witness the destruction of a controlled substance is an example of a:','["discount", "safeguard", "stunt", "delay tactic"]'::jsonb,1,'Witnessing prevents theft.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.E',3,'When putting on PPE, the first item usually put on is the:','["gloves", "bracelet", "gown", "ring"]'::jsonb,2,'Donning order starts with the gown.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.E',4,'When taking off PPE, the contaminated item removed first is the:','["mask", "eye shield", "watch", "gloves"]'::jsonb,3,'Gloves are most contaminated.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.F',3,'Documenting allergies protects a patient from receiving a drug that could cause a:','["reaction", "discount", "reward", "refund"]'::jsonb,0,'Allergy records prevent harm.','original'),
('127.484.d.12.F',4,'Each time a patient picks up a prescription, the technician should ask whether any allergies have:','["been delivered", "changed", "expired", "been sold"]'::jsonb,1,'Allergy lists must stay current.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.A',3,'The branch of pharmacology that studies what a drug does to the body is:','["toxicology only", "pharmacy law", "pharmacodynamics", "pharmacokinetics"]'::jsonb,2,'Pharmacodynamics = drug effects.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.A',4,'Absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion of a drug are studied in:','["pharmacodynamics", "posology", "pharmacognosy", "pharmacokinetics"]'::jsonb,3,'Pharmacokinetics = what the body does to the drug.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.B',3,'An accredited journal article about a clinical trial is an example of a source of drug:','["information", "advertising only", "gossip", "packaging"]'::jsonb,0,'Journals provide evidence.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.B',4,'A drug monograph that lists approved uses, doses, and warnings is also called the package:','["bag", "insert", "box top", "tag"]'::jsonb,1,'Package inserts describe the drug.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.C',3,'A research article reporting original study results is a primary reference, while a textbook that summarizes many studies is a:','["rumor", "primary source again", "tertiary reference", "poster"]'::jsonb,2,'Textbooks are tertiary.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.C',4,'An index that helps find articles by topic without giving the full study is a secondary:','["label", "map", "recipe", "reference"]'::jsonb,3,'Indexes point to primary articles.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.D',3,'The first pharmacists in ancient times prepared remedies from plants, minerals, and:','["animal products", "radios", "computers", "plastics"]'::jsonb,0,'Early medicine used natural materials.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.D',4,'Alexander Fleming''s 1928 discovery of penicillin began the era of modern:','["vaccines for polio", "antibiotics", "vitamins", "anesthetics"]'::jsonb,1,'Penicillin was the first antibiotic.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.E',3,'A drug advertisement states ''9 out of 10 patients felt better'' but does not say how many were studied. This claim lacks:','["music", "humor", "supporting data", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'Ads should be checked against data.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.E',4,'Promotional materials are designed to persuade, so a technician should compare claims to unbiased:','["jingles", "slogans", "coupons", "clinical studies"]'::jsonb,3,'Check claims against evidence.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.F',3,'When a medicine has a very high price, some patients may skip doses, which is a societal impact of drug:','["cost", "color", "smell", "weight"]'::jsonb,0,'High costs affect adherence.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.F',4,'A drug that is made by many companies after the patent ends usually has a lower price than the original brand because of:','["tradition", "competition", "distance", "weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Generic competition lowers cost.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.G',3,'The development of vaccines has reduced deaths from diseases like measles, showing the benefits of scientific:','["rumor", "gossip", "research", "folklore"]'::jsonb,2,'Research improves health.','original'),
('127.485.d.1.G',4,'New drugs are tested in phases of clinical trials to ensure they are both safe and:','["cheap", "fast", "colorful", "effective"]'::jsonb,3,'Trials test safety and efficacy.','original'),
('127.485.d.2.A',3,'A person who wants to dispense medicines in a hospital could become a pharmacist or a pharmacy:','["technician", "pilot", "plumber", "carpenter"]'::jsonb,0,'Pharmacology careers include technicians.','original'),
('127.485.d.2.A',4,'A career path that involves researching new drugs in a lab is a pharmaceutical:','["chef", "scientist", "driver", "clerk"]'::jsonb,1,'Researchers develop drugs.','original'),
('127.485.d.2.B',3,'On a pharmacy team, the person who gives final approval of a filled prescription is the:','["driver", "technician", "pharmacist", "cashier"]'::jsonb,2,'Pharmacists verify.','original'),
('127.485.d.2.B',4,'Pharmacy technicians support pharmacists by handling tasks such as counting, labeling, and:','["surgery", "diagnosing", "prescribing", "data entry"]'::jsonb,3,'Technicians do technical tasks.','original'),
('127.485.d.2.C',3,'A growing area in which pharmacists use genes to choose a drug and dose is called:','["personalized medicine", "fast food", "herbal tea", "aroma care"]'::jsonb,0,'Pharmacogenomics guides therapy.','original'),
('127.485.d.2.C',4,'Pharmacy jobs in nuclear pharmacy handle drugs that contain small amounts of radioactive:','["ink", "material", "sugar", "fabric"]'::jsonb,1,'Nuclear pharmacy prepares radiopharmaceuticals.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.A',3,'A wrong drug given to a patient is a medical error that can result in injury or:','["vacation", "savings", "death", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Errors can have serious consequences.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.A',4,'Common causes of medical errors include poor communication, fatigue, and unclear:','["lighting at night", "weather", "sports", "handwriting"]'::jsonb,3,'Illegible handwriting causes mistakes.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.B',3,'Failing to give the care a reasonable professional would give is called:','["negligence", "luck", "hospitality", "donation"]'::jsonb,0,'Negligence is a failure of duty.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.B',4,'Harm from a professional''s improper conduct that can lead to a lawsuit is called:','["generosity", "malpractice", "kindness", "audit"]'::jsonb,1,'Malpractice is professional negligence.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.C',3,'The ethical principle of doing good for the patient is:','["justice", "negligence", "beneficence", "autonomy"]'::jsonb,2,'Beneficence means doing good.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.C',4,'Respecting a patient''s right to make their own decisions about care is the principle of:','["justice", "beneficence", "fidelity", "autonomy"]'::jsonb,3,'Autonomy is self-determination.','original'),
('127.485.d.3.D',3,'A policy that protects a pharmacist from claims of errors is called professional liability:','["insurance", "patent", "license", "audit"]'::jsonb,0,'Liability coverage protects professionals.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
