('127.485.d.3.D',4,'A technician is responsible for staying within the limits of their training to avoid professional:','["bonus", "liability", "holiday", "reward"]'::jsonb,1,'Liability comes from acts outside scope.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.A',3,'The word root ''cardi'' relates to the:','["kidney", "liver", "heart", "lung"]'::jsonb,2,'Cardi- means heart.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.A',4,'The suffix ''-itis'' means:','["pain relief", "removal", "study", "inflammation"]'::jsonb,3,'-itis = inflammation.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.B',3,'A drug that prevents vomiting is called an anti-:','["emetic", "pyretic", "tussive", "biotic"]'::jsonb,0,'Emetic relates to vomiting.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.B',4,'A diuretic increases the production of:','["bile", "urine", "saliva", "blood"]'::jsonb,1,'Diuretics increase urine output.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.C',3,'Breaking the word ''hypotension'' into parts, ''hypo-'' means:','["around", "without", "below normal", "above normal"]'::jsonb,2,'Hypo = under.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.C',4,'In ''gastroenterology'', ''gastro'' refers to the:','["bone", "brain", "skin", "stomach"]'::jsonb,3,'Gastro = stomach.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.D',3,'A technician explains to a patient that ''hypertension'' means:','["high blood pressure", "low blood sugar", "a stomachache", "a cough"]'::jsonb,0,'Use plain words for patients.','original'),
('127.485.d.4.D',4,'Instead of saying ''take this drug orally,'' a technician can say ''take this by:''','["patch", "mouth", "needle", "ear drop"]'::jsonb,1,'Plain language helps understanding.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.A',3,'A dose of 5 mg per kg for a 40 kg patient is:','["45 mg", "20 mg", "200 mg", "8 mg"]'::jsonb,2,'5 x 40 = 200.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.A',4,'If a 250 mg per 5 mL suspension is available, how many mL contain 500 mg?','["5 mL", "25 mL", "2.5 mL", "10 mL"]'::jsonb,3,'500 / 250 x 5 = 10.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.B',3,'2.5 grams converted to milligrams is:','["2500 mg", "25000 mg", "25 mg", "250 mg"]'::jsonb,0,'Multiply by 1000.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.B',4,'750 mL converted to liters is:','["0.075 L", "0.75 L", "7.5 L", "75 L"]'::jsonb,1,'Divide by 1000.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.C',3,'One ounce is about how many milliliters?','["100 mL", "15 mL", "30 mL", "5 mL"]'::jsonb,2,'1 fl oz = 30 mL.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.C',4,'A patient weighing 110 lb weighs about how many kilograms? (1 kg = 2.2 lb)','["25 kg", "100 kg", "242 kg", "50 kg"]'::jsonb,3,'110 / 2.2 = 50.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.D',3,'Studies show that patients who do not take medicine as directed have poor patient:','["compliance", "grooming", "luck", "income"]'::jsonb,0,'Compliance means following directions.','original'),
('127.485.d.5.D',4,'A statistic from a small sample may not apply to everyone, which is a limitation of:','["font", "sample size", "color", "price"]'::jsonb,1,'Samples limit generalization.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.A',3,'Tablets, capsules, and powders are examples of solid:','["fabrics", "recipes", "dosage forms", "tools"]'::jsonb,2,'Dosage forms vary.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.A',4,'A drug placed on the skin that is absorbed slowly over days is a transdermal:','["tablet", "syrup", "pill", "patch"]'::jsonb,3,'Patches deliver steady doses.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.B',3,'Tylenol is a brand name for the generic drug:','["acetaminophen", "aspirin", "naproxen", "ibuprofen"]'::jsonb,0,'Brand to generic.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.B',4,'Advil is a brand name for the generic drug:','["naproxen", "ibuprofen", "acetaminophen", "aspirin"]'::jsonb,1,'Advil = ibuprofen.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.C',3,'An elixir is a sweet liquid that contains alcohol, while a syrup is a thick sweet:','["powder", "tablet", "liquid with sugar", "patch"]'::jsonb,2,'Syrups contain sugar.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.C',4,'The term ''enteric-coated'' means the tablet is coated to survive stomach acid and dissolve in the:','["eye", "ear", "mouth", "intestine"]'::jsonb,3,'Enteric coating delays release.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.D',3,'An unwanted but expected effect of a drug is a(n):','["side effect", "placebo", "brand name", "therapeutic effect"]'::jsonb,0,'Side effects are secondary.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.D',4,'A harmful drug effect that is not expected at normal doses is a(n):','["refill", "adverse reaction", "therapeutic effect", "order"]'::jsonb,1,'Adverse reactions are dangerous.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.E',3,'Beta blockers work by blocking receptors to slow the:','["growth of hair", "digestion only", "heart rate", "hearing"]'::jsonb,2,'Beta blockers reduce heart rate.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.E',4,'Allergy pills of this type relieve sneezing and itching by blocking the effects of a chemical released in allergic reactions called:','["cortisol", "oxygen", "insulin", "histamine"]'::jsonb,3,'Antihistamines block histamine.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.F',3,'As the dose of a drug increases, the effect usually increases up to a point, which is the dose-response:','["relationship", "budget", "parade", "refill"]'::jsonb,0,'Dose and response are linked.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.F',4,'The dose at which a drug is effective in 50 percent of people is the effective dose 50, while the dose that is lethal in 50 percent is the:','["bonus dose", "lethal dose 50", "minimum dose 50", "safe dose 50"]'::jsonb,1,'LD50 measures toxicity.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.G',3,'A technician practices drug safety by checking expiration dates and storing medicines away from:','["registers", "labels", "children", "pharmacists"]'::jsonb,2,'Keep medicines from kids.','original'),
('127.485.d.6.G',4,'Medicines such as insulin lose strength if they are stored at the wrong:','["noise", "price", "color", "temperature"]'::jsonb,3,'Storage affects potency.','original'),
('127.485.d.7.A',3,'Electronic prescribing, barcode scanning, and robotics are all examples of pharmacy:','["technology", "uniforms", "carpeting", "decor"]'::jsonb,0,'Technology supports workflow.','original'),
('127.485.d.7.A',4,'An electronic health record shares a patient''s medications with the pharmacy to improve:','["parking", "safety", "lunch", "decor"]'::jsonb,1,'EHRs support safe care.','original'),
('127.485.d.7.B',3,'A barcode scan at the time of filling confirms the correct drug and reduces:','["hours", "customers", "errors", "staff"]'::jsonb,2,'Scanning improves accuracy.','original'),
('127.485.d.7.B',4,'Automated refill reminders help patients take medicine regularly, which improves:','["traffic", "profit only", "signage", "adherence"]'::jsonb,3,'Reminders help adherence.','original'),
('127.485.d.7.C',3,'A balance used to weigh compounding ingredients must be regularly calibrated to ensure:','["accuracy", "color", "scent", "noise"]'::jsonb,0,'Calibration keeps it accurate.','original'),
('127.485.d.7.C',4,'Cleaning a counting tray after counting a drug that leaves residue prevents:','["noise", "contamination", "inflation", "fading"]'::jsonb,1,'Residue contaminates.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.A',3,'Workplace safety standards in a pharmacy are set to protect employees from hazards such as chemicals and:','["windows", "clocks", "sharps", "music"]'::jsonb,2,'Safety standards cover hazards.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.A',4,'The agency that sets and enforces workplace safety standards in the United States is OSHA, the Occupational Safety and Health:','["Agreement", "Association", "Alliance", "Administration"]'::jsonb,3,'OSHA enforces standards.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.B',3,'When local and federal rules differ, a pharmacy should follow the:','["strictest rule", "oldest rule", "shortest rule", "loosest rule"]'::jsonb,0,'Stricter standards protect more.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.B',4,'State boards of pharmacy publish rules for pharmacies, and the pharmacy must follow them in addition to federal:','["menus", "law", "fashion", "suggestions"]'::jsonb,1,'Both apply.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.C',3,'Skipping steps like double-checking the label can lead to unsafe practice and:','["bonuses", "awards", "patient harm", "discounts"]'::jsonb,2,'Unsafe practice harms patients.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.C',4,'A pharmacy that repeatedly ignores safety rules may face fines or loss of its:','["mail", "parking", "uniforms", "license"]'::jsonb,3,'Consequences can be severe.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.D',3,'When giving client care, a technician follows procedures that protect both the patient and the:','["caregiver", "calendar", "radio", "budget"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe procedures protect both.','original'),
('127.485.d.8.D',4,'Using sharps safely means never recapping a used needle and disposing of it in a:','["trash can", "sharps container", "drawer", "pocket"]'::jsonb,1,'Sharps containers prevent sticks.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.A',3,'A technician notices that milk left out overnight smells sour and asks what organisms caused the change. This is forming a:','["safety rule", "final grade", "scientific question", "recipe"]'::jsonb,2,'Observations lead to questions.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.A',4,'Before culturing a throat swab, the lab states what is unknown and what will be measured. This step is defining the:','["conclusion", "schedule", "budget", "problem"]'::jsonb,3,'Problems come first.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.B',3,'Growing the same bacteria on plates with and without an antibiotic compares two:','["conditions", "colors", "breeds", "papers"]'::jsonb,0,'Comparative design.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.B',4,'A plate that is left untreated so it can be compared with treated plates is the:','["sample", "control", "variable", "hypothesis"]'::jsonb,1,'Controls provide a baseline.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.C',3,'Used culture plates must be disposed of by sterilizing them in a(n):','["toaster", "freezer", "autoclave", "oven mitt"]'::jsonb,2,'Autoclaves kill microbes.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.C',4,'A spill of bacterial culture on the bench is first covered with paper towels soaked in:','["sand", "soap bubbles", "water only", "disinfectant"]'::jsonb,3,'Disinfect spills.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.D',3,'The tool used to magnify tiny microbes on a slide is a:','["microscope", "ruler", "telescope", "scale"]'::jsonb,0,'Microscopes magnify.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.D',4,'A sterile loop used to transfer bacteria to a plate in a zigzag pattern is called a(n):','["syringe", "inoculating loop", "pipe", "scalpel"]'::jsonb,1,'Loops spread inoculum.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.E',3,'The width of a bacterial cell is measured in micrometers, a unit in the:','["imperial yards", "US customary system", "International System of Units", "random units"]'::jsonb,2,'SI includes micrometers.','original'),
('127.486.d.1.E',4,'A colony measuring 3 mm is how many micrometers wide?','["30", "300", "0.3", "3000"]'::jsonb,3,'1 mm = 1000 micrometers.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
