from (values
('127.486.d.7.D',4,'A larger zone of inhibition around a disc generally means the bacteria are more:','["colorful", "numerous", "resistant", "susceptible"]'::jsonb,3,'Bigger zone = more sensitive.','original'),
('127.486.d.7.E',3,'Travel, crowded living, and poor sanitation can contribute to the emergence of:','["new infectious diseases", "stock sales", "new snacks", "fashion"]'::jsonb,0,'Social factors matter.','original'),
('127.486.d.7.E',4,'A disease that was nearly gone and has returned is described as:','["emerging only", "reemerging", "extinct", "chronic"]'::jsonb,1,'Reemerging diseases return.','original'),
('127.486.d.7.F',3,'MRSA is resistant to methicillin and many other:','["vitamins", "vaccines", "antibiotics", "enzymes"]'::jsonb,2,'MRSA resists antibiotics.','original'),
('127.486.d.7.F',4,'Overusing antibiotics encourages the survival of the most:','["sensitive bacteria", "vitamins", "viruses only", "resistant bacteria"]'::jsonb,3,'Resistant strains survive.','original'),
('127.486.d.7.G',3,'The World Health Organization monitors disease worldwide and sets:','["health guidelines", "fashion trends", "sports rules", "menu prices"]'::jsonb,0,'WHO sets guidelines.','original'),
('127.486.d.7.G',4,'In the United States, outbreaks of reportable diseases are tracked by local and state health departments and the:','["NFL", "CDC", "NBA", "NASA"]'::jsonb,1,'CDC collects reports.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.A',3,'Treating all blood and body fluids as if they could spread infection is called standard:','["rewards", "recipes", "precautions", "reminders"]'::jsonb,2,'Standard precautions.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.A',4,'A lab worker with a cut on the hand should cover it with a waterproof bandage and wear:','["bracelets", "a scarf", "rings", "gloves"]'::jsonb,3,'Protect broken skin.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.B',3,'The four biosafety levels classify labs according to the risk of the microbes handled, with BSL-1 being the:','["lowest risk", "highest risk", "largest", "most expensive"]'::jsonb,0,'BSL-1 is lowest.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.B',4,'Mouth pipetting is never allowed because it can cause you to swallow:','["a ruler", "a sample", "a pencil", "a plate"]'::jsonb,1,'Use pipette aids.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.C',3,'Gloves, goggles, and a lab coat are examples of personal protective:','["opinions", "schedules", "equipment", "recipes"]'::jsonb,2,'PPE protects workers.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.C',4,'After a lab session, you should remove your gloves and then wash your hands with:','["juice", "dry paper", "sand", "soap and water"]'::jsonb,3,'Hand hygiene follows PPE removal.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.D',3,'Surgical instruments are sterilized using steam under pressure in an:','["autoclave", "oven", "toaster", "fridge"]'::jsonb,0,'Autoclaves use pressure.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.D',4,'To confirm an autoclave worked, labs use indicator tape or biological indicators containing resistant:','["crystals", "spores", "leaves", "seeds"]'::jsonb,1,'Spores show effectiveness.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.E',3,'A chemical that can be safely used on living tissue to slow microbes is an:','["detergent", "bleach", "antiseptic", "disinfectant for floors"]'::jsonb,2,'Antiseptics are for skin.','original'),
('127.486.d.8.E',4,'A chemical used on surfaces and objects, not skin, to kill microbes is a:','["antibiotic", "antiseptic", "vitamin", "disinfectant"]'::jsonb,3,'Disinfectants are for objects.','original'),
('127.487.d.1.A',3,'A system that stores and manages a patient''s medical history in digital form is a(n):','["electronic health record", "recipe card", "paper chart", "phone book"]'::jsonb,0,'EHRs store records digitally.','original'),
('127.487.d.1.A',4,'A hospital''s laboratory information system is designed specifically to manage:','["parking", "lab test orders and results", "menus", "payroll only"]'::jsonb,1,'LIS handles lab data.','original'),
('127.487.d.1.B',3,'Health information systems help administrators track patient visits, billing, and hospital:','["gossip", "fashion", "resources", "music"]'::jsonb,2,'Systems support administration.','original'),
('127.487.d.1.B',4,'Dashboards that show how many beds are open help hospital staff make decisions about:','["landscaping", "art", "wardrobe", "patient flow"]'::jsonb,3,'Data supports operations.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.A',3,'Software that lets users create, store, and retrieve data in a database is a database:','["management system", "decoration", "alarm", "hobby"]'::jsonb,0,'A DBMS organizes data.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.A',4,'A database management system lets many users search and update records while controlling who may:','["delete the building", "access them", "print money", "change the weather"]'::jsonb,1,'DBMS controls access.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.B',3,'Planning how data will be organized in a database before building it is the purpose of data:','["guessing", "erasing", "modeling", "storage"]'::jsonb,2,'Modeling plans structure.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.B',4,'A data model helps designers show how pieces of information are connected so that the database is easier to:','["delete", "ignore", "hide", "use and maintain"]'::jsonb,3,'Models clarify design.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.C',3,'The customary first step in data modeling is to identify the data that must be:','["stored", "hidden", "ignored", "erased"]'::jsonb,0,'Start with requirements.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.C',4,'After identifying the data needed, designers create diagrams that show the entities and then build the:','["vending machine", "database structure", "menu", "calendar"]'::jsonb,1,'Modeling moves from concept to implementation.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.D',3,'In a patient table, a person such as ''patient'' is an entity, and a piece of information like ''birth date'' is an:','["entity", "server", "attribute", "relationship"]'::jsonb,2,'Attributes describe entities.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.D',4,'The link between a patient and the doctors who treat that patient is a:','["attribute", "password", "backup", "relationship"]'::jsonb,3,'Relationships connect entities.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.E',3,'A hospital stores its records in a system owned and used within the organization, called an organizational:','["database", "bookshelf", "stock market", "toolbox"]'::jsonb,0,'Organizations keep databases.','original'),
('127.487.d.2.E',4,'A database stored on remote servers and accessed over the internet is a(n):','["paper database", "cloud database", "hallway database", "tape rack"]'::jsonb,1,'Cloud storage is remote.','original'),
('127.487.d.3.A',3,'Making sure that health data is not changed without permission is called data:','["gossip", "delay", "integrity", "display"]'::jsonb,2,'Integrity means accuracy and protection.','original'),
('127.487.d.3.A',4,'Using unique usernames and passwords helps keep health data:','["public", "random", "shared", "secure"]'::jsonb,3,'Security needs authentication.','original'),
('127.487.d.3.B',3,'Information that a nurse enters in a patient''s chart should be accurate, complete, and:','["timely", "optional", "colorful", "creative"]'::jsonb,0,'Data should be timely.','original'),
('127.487.d.3.B',4,'Backing up health records regularly helps protect them from loss due to:','["a day off", "system failure", "rain on the sidewalk", "a new hairstyle"]'::jsonb,1,'Backups protect data.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.A',3,'The shift from paper charts to digital records has grown rapidly because it can improve patient safety and:','["clutter", "errors", "efficiency", "delays"]'::jsonb,2,'EHRs support efficiency.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.A',4,'A major benefit of an EHR is that a patient''s information can be accessed by authorized providers at:','["only at night", "only one desk", "only on paper", "multiple locations"]'::jsonb,3,'EHRs increase access.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.B',3,'The federal HITECH Act encouraged health care providers to adopt electronic:','["health records", "uniforms", "recipes", "menus"]'::jsonb,0,'HITECH promoted EHRs.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.B',4,'Before EHRs became common, patient information was mostly kept on:','["clouds", "paper", "tape", "hard drives"]'::jsonb,1,'Paper charts came first.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.C',3,'A functional requirement of an EHR is that it must let providers enter orders, view results, and:','["hide notes", "throw away data", "document care", "change patients"]'::jsonb,2,'Documentation is core.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.C',4,'A basic EHR requirement is that every action in the record is logged with a:','["joke", "weather note", "color code", "user and time stamp"]'::jsonb,3,'Audit trails are required.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.D',3,'The ability of different health IT systems to exchange and use information is called:','["interoperability", "isolation", "compression", "redundancy"]'::jsonb,0,'Systems must communicate.','original'),
('127.487.d.4.D',4,'Interoperability is important because a patient may be treated by providers who use different:','["floors", "software systems", "parking decks", "uniforms"]'::jsonb,1,'Interoperability shares data.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.A',3,'The law that protects the privacy of patient health information is the Health Insurance Portability and:','["Assistance Act", "Allocation Act", "Accountability Act", "Approval Act"]'::jsonb,2,'HIPAA protects PHI.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.A',4,'Under HIPAA, patient information may be shared without a signed release for treatment, payment, and health care:','["parties", "gossip", "advertising", "operations"]'::jsonb,3,'TPO exceptions.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.B',3,'Billing for services that were never provided is insurance:','["fraud", "abuse", "rebate", "audit"]'::jsonb,0,'Fraud is intentional deception.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.B',4,'Billing practices that are inconsistent with sound practice but not intentionally deceptive are insurance:','["fraud", "abuse", "adjudication", "coding"]'::jsonb,1,'Abuse is not necessarily intentional.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.C',3,'CPT codes describe the medical procedures and services that were:','["canceled", "imagined", "performed", "rumored"]'::jsonb,2,'CPT codes identify services.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.C',4,'A claim links a CPT code with a diagnosis code to show the service was medically:','["funny", "optional", "free", "necessary"]'::jsonb,3,'Linking shows necessity.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.D',3,'The ICD-10-CM code system is used to code a patient''s:','["diagnosis", "favorite food", "height only", "address"]'::jsonb,0,'ICD codes diagnoses.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.D',4,'To select the correct ICD-10-CM code, a coder starts with the diagnosis in the physician''s documentation and looks it up in the:','["dictionary of slang", "alphabetic index", "street map", "phone book"]'::jsonb,1,'Index leads to the tabular list.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.E',3,'HCPCS codes have two levels: Level I is CPT codes, and Level II covers supplies and services such as:','["movie tickets", "haircuts", "ambulance rides", "groceries"]'::jsonb,2,'Level II covers non-physician services.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.E',4,'Level II HCPCS codes begin with a:','["symbol", "number", "space", "letter"]'::jsonb,3,'Level II codes start with a letter.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.F',3,'Incorrect medical coding can cause claims to be:','["denied", "admired", "celebrated", "framed"]'::jsonb,0,'Coding errors cause denials.','original'),
('127.487.d.5.F',4,'Accurate coding helps ensure that the provider receives the proper:','["vacation", "payment", "trophy", "promotion"]'::jsonb,1,'Coding affects reimbursement.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
