('127.487.d.6.A',3,'An organization that processes Medicare claims for a region is called a fiscal:','["patient", "customer", "intermediary", "vendor"]'::jsonb,2,'FIs process claims.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.A',4,'A fiscal intermediary acts as a link between the government program and the:','["bank teller", "school", "grocery store", "health care provider"]'::jsonb,3,'FIs connect providers and payers.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.B',3,'The federal health insurance program primarily for people age 65 and older is:','["Medicare", "Medicaid", "TRICARE", "CHIP"]'::jsonb,0,'Medicare covers seniors.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.B',4,'The joint federal and state program that helps cover medical costs for people with low income is:','["TRICARE", "Medicaid", "COBRA", "Medicare"]'::jsonb,1,'Medicaid is income-based.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.C',3,'The health care program for active-duty military members and their families is:','["Medicare", "Medicaid", "TRICARE", "CHIP"]'::jsonb,2,'TRICARE serves the military.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.C',4,'CHAMPVA provides health care benefits to dependents of veterans who are:','["retired from school", "healthy", "uninsured only", "permanently and totally disabled"]'::jsonb,3,'CHAMPVA serves certain families.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.D',3,'A health insurance claim for an injury that happened on the job is usually handled under:','["workers'' compensation", "Medicare Part D", "dental insurance", "auto insurance"]'::jsonb,0,'Work injuries go to workers'' comp.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.D',4,'In a workers'' compensation case, the employer is usually required to be notified of the injury within a set:','["century", "time period", "season", "hour of the day"]'::jsonb,1,'Deadlines apply.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.E',3,'The standard paper claim form used by many professional providers is the:','["UB-04 for hospitals only", "W-2", "CMS-1500", "IRS-1040"]'::jsonb,2,'CMS-1500 is the professional claim.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.E',4,'On the CMS-1500 form, Block 21 lists the ICD codes. This block records the patient''s medical:','["address", "employer", "birthday", "diagnosis"]'::jsonb,3,'Block 21 is diagnoses.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.F',3,'Claims can be transmitted electronically through direct entry, a clearinghouse, or a payer:','["portal", "carrier pigeon", "fax only", "bulletin board"]'::jsonb,0,'Portals transmit claims.','original'),
('127.487.d.6.F',4,'A company that checks claims for errors and forwards them to insurers is a:','["greenhouse", "clearinghouse", "warehouse", "newsstand"]'::jsonb,1,'Clearinghouses scrub claims.','original'),
('127.488.d.1.A',3,'A job that involves assigning codes to diagnoses and procedures is a medical:','["pilot", "welder", "coder", "chef"]'::jsonb,2,'Coders assign codes.','original'),
('127.488.d.1.A',4,'A professional who submits claims and follows up on unpaid insurance claims works in medical:','["surgery", "dentistry", "radiology", "billing"]'::jsonb,3,'Billers manage claims.','original'),
('127.488.d.1.B',3,'Coding a service that was not provided in order to be paid more is unethical and is a form of:','["fraud", "charity", "audit", "training"]'::jsonb,0,'Ethical coding is honest.','original'),
('127.488.d.1.B',4,'Professional associations publish codes of ethics that require members to code from the physician''s:','["rumors", "documentation", "guesses", "opinions"]'::jsonb,1,'Code only what is documented.','original'),
('127.488.d.1.C',3,'The American Academy of Professional Coders (AAPC) and the American Health Information Management Association (AHIMA) are professional:','["airlines", "banks", "associations", "stores"]'::jsonb,2,'Both are associations.','original'),
('127.488.d.1.C',4,'Earning a credential such as CPC shows that a coder has passed a certification:','["parade", "tournament", "contest", "exam"]'::jsonb,3,'Credentials need exams.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.A',3,'The agency that runs Medicare and Medicaid is the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid:','["Services", "Supplies", "Systems", "Studies"]'::jsonb,0,'CMS runs the programs.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.A',4,'The federal office that investigates health care fraud and publishes an exclusion list is the Office of Inspector:','["Standards", "General", "Safety", "Services"]'::jsonb,1,'OIG investigates fraud.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.B',3,'The Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act sets rules for the privacy and security of patient:','["bank accounts", "car records", "health information", "school grades"]'::jsonb,2,'HIPAA covers PHI.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.B',4,'The False Claims Act imposes penalties on those who knowingly submit false claims to:','["a friend", "a pet store", "a neighbor", "the government"]'::jsonb,3,'FCA covers government payers.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.C',3,'A coder who sees that a physician''s note does not support a billed service should notify a supervisor, which is an example of ethical:','["behavior", "delay", "hesitation", "failure"]'::jsonb,0,'Report discrepancies.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.C',4,'Using a different code than the documentation supports in order to get a higher payment is a legal and ethical:','["best practice", "violation", "shortcut allowed", "courtesy"]'::jsonb,1,'Upcoding is illegal.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.D',3,'A medical office follows a written plan to make sure it obeys rules and laws, called a compliance:','["menu", "contest", "program", "party"]'::jsonb,2,'Compliance programs prevent violations.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.D',4,'Regular internal audits of claims are one element of a compliance:','["cleanup", "trend", "joke", "plan"]'::jsonb,3,'Audits detect errors.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.E',3,'Before a medical office sends a patient''s records to another office for non-treatment purposes, it generally needs a signed:','["release form", "receipt", "greeting card", "gift note"]'::jsonb,0,'Authorization is required.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.E',4,'A release of information authorization must state what information is being released and to:','["when the sun sets", "whom", "how far it is", "why the doctor is tall"]'::jsonb,1,'Authorizations name the recipient.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.F',3,'A patient who signs a document agreeing to a surgery has given:','["no consent", "verbal denial", "informed consent", "implied consent"]'::jsonb,2,'Informed consent is documented.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.F',4,'A patient who rolls up a sleeve and offers an arm for a shot is showing:','["written consent", "no consent", "informed consent", "implied consent"]'::jsonb,3,'Actions imply agreement.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.G',3,'Sharing patient information inside the office for treatment is a use of information, while sending it to an outside party is a:','["disclosure", "repair", "deletion", "correction"]'::jsonb,0,'Use is internal, disclosure is external.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.G',4,'Telling a billing company about a patient''s diagnosis so it can file a claim is a disclosure that is permitted for:','["gossip", "payment", "entertainment", "marketing"]'::jsonb,1,'Payment is a permitted purpose.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.H',3,'A review of a case in which a provider billed twice for the same visit would look for possible insurance:','["generosity", "luck", "fraud or abuse", "bonuses"]'::jsonb,2,'Duplicate billing is a red flag.','original'),
('127.488.d.2.H',4,'Billing for a more expensive service than was performed is called:','["rounding", "downcoding", "unbundling only", "upcoding"]'::jsonb,3,'Upcoding inflates payment.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.B',3,'A diagnosis such as depression, ADHD, or autism spectrum disorder is classified in ICD-10-CM among mental, behavioral, and neurodevelopmental:','["disorders", "devices", "supplies", "procedures"]'::jsonb,0,'Chapter F covers these conditions.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.B',4,'A coder finds ''bipolar disorder'' in a note. This diagnosis is located in the ICD-10-CM chapter for mental, behavioral, and neurodevelopmental:','["devices", "disorders", "supplies", "factors"]'::jsonb,1,'Chapter 5 (F codes) holds mood disorders.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.i',3,'Coders classify skin conditions such as eczema and burns under the body system called the:','["urinary system", "skeletal system", "integumentary system", "nervous system"]'::jsonb,2,'The skin is the integumentary system.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.i',4,'The outermost layer of skin that coders may see named in documentation is the:','["pericardium", "pleura", "meninges", "epidermis"]'::jsonb,3,'The epidermis is the outer layer.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.ii',3,'A fracture of the femur is coded under conditions of the:','["skeletal system", "urinary system", "endocrine system", "respiratory system"]'::jsonb,0,'Bones belong to the skeletal system.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.ii',4,'The ICD-10-CM chapter for diseases of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissue includes arthritis, which affects the:','["kidneys", "joints", "lungs", "eyes"]'::jsonb,1,'Arthritis is joint inflammation.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.iii',3,'The system that includes tendons and the biceps, which coders must be able to identify in documentation, is the:','["lymphatic system", "urinary system", "muscular system", "digestive system"]'::jsonb,2,'Muscles move the body.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.iii',4,'A coder sees ''myalgia'' in a note. This term means:','["blood clot", "skin rash", "bone pain", "muscle pain"]'::jsonb,3,'Myo = muscle; algia = pain.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.iv',3,'A coder assigning a code for a heart attack uses the chapter for diseases of the circulatory system, also called the:','["cardiovascular system", "skeletal system", "integumentary system", "digestive system"]'::jsonb,0,'The heart is part of the cardiovascular system.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.iv',4,'The medical term for a high blood pressure diagnosis that a coder might find in a note is:','["hypotension", "hypertension", "tachycardia", "arrhythmia"]'::jsonb,1,'Hypertension = high pressure.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.v',3,'Pneumonia and asthma are coded in the chapter for diseases of the:','["skeletal system", "circulatory system", "respiratory system", "nervous system"]'::jsonb,2,'Lungs are respiratory.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.v',4,'The term ''dyspnea'' in a physician''s note means:','["chest pain", "stomach pain", "fast heartbeat", "difficulty breathing"]'::jsonb,3,'Dys = difficult, pnea = breathing.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.vi',3,'Coders assign codes for appendicitis and ulcers under diseases of the:','["digestive system", "nervous system", "respiratory system", "urinary system"]'::jsonb,0,'The GI tract is digestive.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.vi',4,'The word ''gastritis'' refers to inflammation of the:','["kidney", "stomach lining", "pancreas only", "liver"]'::jsonb,1,'Gastr = stomach.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.vii',3,'Diabetes mellitus is coded under endocrine, nutritional, and metabolic diseases because it involves the hormone:','["adrenaline", "estrogen", "insulin", "thyroid only"]'::jsonb,2,'Diabetes involves insulin.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.vii',4,'A gland in the neck that regulates metabolism, coded under the endocrine system, is the:','["spleen", "tonsil", "liver", "thyroid"]'::jsonb,3,'The thyroid is endocrine.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.viii',3,'A urinary tract infection and kidney stones are coded under diseases of the:','["genitourinary system", "respiratory system", "digestive system", "integumentary system"]'::jsonb,0,'ICD groups them as genitourinary.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.viii',4,'The organs that filter blood and produce urine, whose diseases coders must recognize, are the:','["lymph nodes", "kidneys", "lungs", "tonsils"]'::jsonb,1,'Kidneys form urine.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.ix',3,'Pregnancy, childbirth, and the puerperium have their own chapter, and coders must understand the female:','["muscular system", "respiratory system", "reproductive system", "skeletal system"]'::jsonb,2,'Obstetrics is reproductive.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.ix',4,'The male gland that sits below the bladder and can be coded for enlargement is the:','["thyroid", "pancreas", "spleen", "prostate"]'::jsonb,3,'BPH involves the prostate.','original'),
('127.488.d.3.A.x',3,'Codes for stroke, epilepsy, and migraine fall under diseases of the:','["nervous system", "skeletal system", "digestive system", "urinary system"]'::jsonb,0,'The brain is nervous system.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_72_v1'
from (values
('127.488.d.3.A.x',4,'The sense organs, such as the eye and ear, are included in the ICD-10-CM chapters on diseases of the eye and adnexa and of the:','["heart and aorta", "ear and mastoid process", "foot and ankle", "hair and nails"]'::jsonb,1,'Special senses have chapters.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.A',3,'Coding conventions and guidelines help a coder record every billable service, a task called charge:','["delay", "erase", "capture", "theft"]'::jsonb,2,'Charge capture ensures billing.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.A',4,'Following the official ICD-10-CM guidelines ensures that diagnosis codes are assigned:','["creatively", "slowly", "randomly", "consistently"]'::jsonb,3,'Guidelines promote consistency.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.B',3,'Coding manuals are revised every year, so coders must regularly update their:','["code books", "chairs", "uniforms", "lunch boxes"]'::jsonb,0,'Annual updates occur.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.B',4,'ICD-10-CM updates take effect each year on:','["December 25", "October 1", "January 1", "July 4"]'::jsonb,1,'ICD-10-CM updates start in October.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.C',3,'Coding to the highest level of specificity means choosing the code with the most:','["letters only", "cost", "detail", "brevity"]'::jsonb,2,'Specific codes are preferred.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.C',4,'A coder should assign a code only when the physician has documented the diagnosis, not when it is only:','["treated", "charted", "confirmed", "suspected in outpatient coding"]'::jsonb,3,'Outpatient rules exclude uncertain diagnoses.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.D',3,'Diagnosis-related groups classify hospital patients into groups for payment, which is an example of disease:','["groupings", "guesses", "menus", "mailings"]'::jsonb,0,'DRGs group by diagnosis.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.D',4,'Combining several related procedure codes into one comprehensive code for billing is called:','["splitting", "bundling", "unbundling", "dropping"]'::jsonb,1,'Bundling combines.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.E',3,'A payer will cover a service only if it is medically:','["decorative", "free", "necessary", "optional"]'::jsonb,2,'Medical necessity justifies payment.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.E',4,'A national coverage determination from Medicare explains which services are covered based on medical:','["geography", "fashion", "opinion", "necessity"]'::jsonb,3,'NCDs outline necessity.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.F',3,'The abbreviation ''NPO'' on a chart means:','["nothing by mouth", "normal pulse only", "next patient overdue", "no pain observed"]'::jsonb,0,'NPO = nil per os.','original'),
('127.488.d.4.F',4,'The abbreviation ''CHF'' stands for congestive:','["health fund", "heart failure", "hearing fault", "hip fracture"]'::jsonb,1,'CHF = congestive heart failure.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.A',3,'The process of tracking patient care from scheduling to final payment is revenue cycle:','["decoration", "cleaning", "management", "marketing"]'::jsonb,2,'RCM covers the whole payment process.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.A',4,'A medical office''s revenue cycle begins at patient scheduling and ends when the account is:','["deleted", "framed", "ignored", "paid in full"]'::jsonb,3,'RCM ends at payment.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.B',3,'A plan offered through a person''s job is an employer-sponsored plan, while Medicaid is a government:','["program", "club", "lottery", "coupon"]'::jsonb,0,'Government plans exist.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.B',4,'A plan that requires patients to choose a primary care provider and get referrals to see specialists is a(n):','["FSA", "HMO", "HSA", "PPO"]'::jsonb,1,'HMOs use gatekeepers.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.C',3,'An insurance company that processes Medicare claims for a geographic region is a Medicare Administrative:','["Cashier", "Customer", "Contractor", "Competitor"]'::jsonb,2,'MACs process claims.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.C',4,'MACs also educate providers about Medicare rules and process provider:','["lunches", "uniforms", "vacations", "appeals"]'::jsonb,3,'MACs support providers.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.D',3,'At check-in, the front desk copies the patient''s insurance card and verifies:','["eligibility", "height", "hobbies", "birth month only"]'::jsonb,0,'Verify coverage.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.D',4,'Collecting a copay at the time of check-in is part of the:','["billing audit only", "patient registration process", "lab process", "coding process only"]'::jsonb,1,'Front-end collection.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.E',3,'The block on the CMS-1500 form that lists the patient''s insurance ID number is in the section for:','["supplies", "lab results", "insured information", "parking"]'::jsonb,2,'Insurance info is on the form.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.E',4,'When preparing a mock claim, the biller enters the provider''s National Provider Identifier, abbreviated:','["SSN", "ZIP", "PIN", "NPI"]'::jsonb,3,'NPI identifies providers.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.F',3,'When a patient has two insurance plans, the plan billed first is the:','["primary plan", "secondary plan", "backup plan", "dental plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Primary pays first.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.F',4,'The plan that pays after the primary plan has paid is the:','["primary plan", "secondary plan", "first plan", "main plan"]'::jsonb,1,'Secondary covers remaining costs.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.G',3,'A document from an insurer explaining how a claim was paid is the remittance:','["rumor", "invoice for lunch", "advice", "menu"]'::jsonb,2,'Remittance advice explains payment.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.G',4,'On a remittance advice, the amount the patient owes after the insurer pays is the patient:','["vacation", "bonus", "discount", "responsibility"]'::jsonb,3,'Patient responsibility is the balance.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.H',3,'A claim returned because of an error, such as a missing signature, is a(n):','["rejection", "payment", "approval", "bonus"]'::jsonb,0,'Rejections need corrections.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.H',4,'A denial because a service is not covered can be addressed by filing a(n):','["greeting", "appeal", "reminder", "receipt"]'::jsonb,1,'Appeals contest denials.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.I',3,'A listing that groups unpaid claims by how long they have been outstanding is an aging:','["brochure", "menu", "report", "poster"]'::jsonb,2,'Aging reports show past-due claims.','original'),
('127.488.d.5.I',4,'Claims in the 90-plus days column of an aging report are the ones most at risk of not being:','["filed", "printed", "coded", "collected"]'::jsonb,3,'Older accounts are harder to collect.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
